  "body": "With several setups on screen, every origin triad looks alike - nothing in the viewport says whose zero is whose (#727).\n\n## The change\n\nEvery origin gizmo now labels itself at its origin. Each work-offset triad draws the entity name the Setup pane already uses (`G54` for the first setup, `Setup2/WCS` for the second) in bright triad blue at the ordinary overlay-label size; the dimmed world axes draw `World` in neutral gray dimmed by `WORLD_DIM`, like the lines under them. `Gizmo` (`interact.rs`) grows one `name` field, filled in `gizmos()` - which already honors the Models pane's eye (`hidden_offsets`) and the `show_world_axes` gate, so a hidden offset loses its name with its lines for free. `overlay_labels` places each name just below the projected origin (`NAME_DROP_UV = 0.02`, same currency as `axis_note::NOTE_DROP_UV`), emitted before the gizmo's `X`/`Y`/`Z` tips. Only the letters keep the big `is_axis_label` font. Rationale in `docs/decisions/727-viewport-gizmo-labels.md`.\n\n## The switch (#645)\n\nOn top of the names, the review on #645 asked for a user switch, so the browser pane grows a `Show origin names` checkbox next to `Show world origin axes`. It gates only the name rows: the big `X`/`Y`/`Z` letters and the triad's strokes ignore it. The choice is a per-user preference, not document state - nothing touches the world or the command history - and it persists in `view.json` in the OS config folder next to the recents file (`recent`'s resolver, #662, so `CAMCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR` overrides the folder), written at once on the flip and read back at startup. The default is ON, the #727 decision: shipping the switch changes no existing viewport. A missing, unreadable or corrupt file - or a foreign one, the `camcraft-view/1` format tag says - starts at the defaults with a logged reason, never a crash, and unknown keys stay ignored so newer builds keep working.\n\n## Pins (red on main, green with the fix)\n\n- `gizmo_tests::the_dimmed_world_axes_are_labelled_world` - the fresh world's set carries `World`, neutral gray (equal channels) and dimmed like the axes.\n- `gizmo_tests::each_triad_is_labelled_with_its_own_offset_name` - two setups: both `G54` and `Setup2/WCS` label their own origins, bright against the letters.\n- `gizmo_tests::an_offset_name_stands_at_its_origin_not_its_axis_tips` - the name rides the projected origin horizontally, a small uv drop below it, not crowded onto the tips.\n- `gizmo_tests::a_hidden_work_offset_drops_its_name_with_its_gizmo` - the pane's eye and the label agree.\n- `gizmo_tests::gizmo_names_are_not_the_big_axis_letters` - `is_axis_label` still answers only X/Y/Z.\n- Re-pins: label counts 3→4 (fresh world), 6→8 (two gizmos), 3→4 (moved origin); `axis_note_tests`' fresh-world set pins exactly `[\"World\", \"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"]`, which fixes each gizmo's emission order name-first.\n- `setup_chip_tests`' no-G54-on-Setup2's-op clause narrows to plane chips (`\" · \"`): the `G54` origin name is Setup1's own, legitimately - the law was about op chips, and it still holds there.\n- `structural::origin_names_paint_on_and_quiet_off_letters_and_lines_always` - the re-review's both-states shell check: with the switch on the seeded document's `G54` name row paints inside the viewport (the properties pane also reads `G54`, so the probe sits between the pane anchors, as the view-cube check does); the checkbox click drops it from the painted frame while the `X`/`Y`/`Z` letters and the triad's strokes come through untouched. The test redirects `view_store` to a temp folder so the flip never writes the real user's `view.json`.\n- `crates/app/tests/view_prefs.rs` (new integration suite) - the persistence law: a flipped choice round-trips through the file across a \"restart\", a missing file is a quiet default start, a corrupt or foreign-format file starts at the defaults with a reason and never crashes, unknown keys stay ignored, and a `CAMCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR` override is the folder the choice round-trips through (`recent::config_dir_for` with a fake getter, as `recent_files` does).\n\n## Tested\n\n- Red first: with only the pins committed, `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- gizmo_tests axis_note_tests` ran 8 failed / 7 passed, exactly the new and re-pinned label tests - e.g. the fresh world's labels were `[\"X\", \"Y\", \"Z\"]` with no name.\n- Green: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- gizmo_tests axis_note_tests setup_chip_tests` - 17 passed, 0 failed.\n- Full lib: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` - 490 passed, 0 failed (5 ignored). An earlier run of the same command failed only on `structural::shell_structure_light`, a theme-sync test this change never touches; it passes in isolation and on re-run - pre-existing parallel global-theme-state flakiness, already noted on #638.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test view_prefs` - 5 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` - clean.\n- Not exercised: the on-screen labels themselves - the producers are pinned instead.\n\nChangelog: viewport origin gizmos now wear their names - each work-offset triad shows its Setup-pane name at its origin, the neutral world axes show World (#727) - and a persisted \"Show origin names\" checkbox in the browser pane turns the name rows on and off, kept in the per-user `view.json` (#645)\n\nFixes #727\n",
